From: F93k draft audit
Subject: [test-control] hold failed-close owner loop through release assertion

Evidence-only correction for F93jQuicFailedDialResourceTest. Each failed dial's physical-close completion listener fails the original close promise, signals the caller, and then holds the owning event loop. The caller checks the dial is still pending and attempts to bind the exact UDP address while the loop is held. A per-cycle finally releases the gate before the existing dial result, close-state, rebind, descriptor, probe, and shutdown assertions. The 128 measured cycles and existing bounds remain unchanged. This tests native release ordering; it does not claim bounded Java failure history.

---
